id: SEC-020
title: LDAP filter injection (CVE-2017-8028)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .java .kt .cs .php .py
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
  content_contains: ldap
patterns:
  - regex: ldap_search\(.*\$_(GET|POST|REQUEST)
    message: User input in ldap_search() — LDAP injection enables auth bypass and data exfiltration
  - regex: search_s\(.*format\(
    message: Python format string in LDAP search — LDAP injection risk
  - regex: search_s\(.*\+\s*['"]
    message: String concatenation in LDAP search — LDAP injection risk
fix: Use parameterized LDAP filters. Escape special chars with ldap_filter_encode (PHP) or ldap3.utils.dn.escape_rdn (Python).
